    "narrative": "The Zurich Zebras enter the July 25th slate with a core anchored by **Christian Yelich**, our highest-rated option at a 75.84, who benefits immensely from a plus-matchup against Ryan Feltner; his elite platoon advantage (13%) and leadoff status make him a must-start for maximizing our R and SB potential. **Junior Caminero** (69.49) and **Colt Keith** (68.51) represent our most consistent offensive threats today, with both capitalizing on favorable lineup positioning and exploitable starting pitching to maintain high daily efficiency. While **Pete Crow-Armstrong** faces a difficult assignment against Paul Skenes, his dynamic platoon edge and top-of-the-order usage keep his score in the strong range, ensuring he remains essential for stolen base volume despite the elite opposing arm.\n\nOur most difficult roster decision involved keeping **Caleb Durbin** on the bench. Despite a solid base projection, his score of 44.94 was ultimately dragged down by a sub-optimal matchup against Dylan Cease. The optimizer favored the immediate offensive ceiling of **Casey Schmitt** (63.92), whose strong SP skill rating and wind-aided park factor provided a safer statistical floor. We are proceeding with caution regarding **Dillon Dingler**, **Gary Sanchez**, **Kazuma Okamoto**, **Chase Meidroth**, **Trea Turner**, **Yordan Alvarez**, **Carson Benge**, and **Kyle Schwarber**, as all remain in \"Lineup Pending\" status. Owners should monitor weather reports and official lineups closely, specifically regarding **Carson Benge**, who draws the toughest assignment of the day against Yoshinobu Yamamoto and carries the lowest score among our starters at 45.49. We continue to track **Lars Nootbaar**, **Nelson Velazquez**, **Josh Smith**, **Jacob Gonzalez**, **Luis Pena**, and **Pedro Ramirez** for potential late-week pivots, while **Hyeseong Kim** remains inactive in the minors.",
